      "type": "state-timeline",
      "title": "$service assertions",
      "description": "Firing SAAFE alerts scoped to the selected service (same pattern as the Assertions dashboard's Timeline row). cdm_source=~\"^($source|)$\" scopes alerts that carry a cdm_source label (HighErrorRate, AnomalyDetected) to the selected $source, while still showing alerts with no cdm_source label at all (VersionUpdated, InstanceDown, InstanceRestarted, the saturation alerts) regardless of which $source is selected, since they have no source to filter by. Not a hardcoded alertname list: any alert whose series carries a service label matches. Queries ALERTS directly with no sum by(...) wrapper: several alerts can legitimately fire more than once concurrently under the same alertname, distinguished only by a label an aggregation would otherwise discard (HighErrorRate by cdm_source, AnomalyDetected by anomaly_name, VersionUpdated by saafe_version_type/saafe_source) -- aggregating would silently sum those into one row with value 2+, breaking the \"1\" -> \"firing\" mapping and hiding that two independent things are happening. Unaggregated, every concurrent instance gets its own row and is always exactly 1.",
